Distrusts the eight eMudhra intermediate CAs whose private keys were computable from their certificates
(October 2026, Mozilla bug 2083449), in the engine itself rather than through the CRLSet component: their
eight SPKI SHA-256 hashes join kSPKIBlockList, which covers each intermediate and its Sectigo cross-sign,
and so does the SPKI of their root, "emSign ECC Root CA - G3", which also leaves the compiled Chrome Root Store
(Chrome Root Store v43 removes it). The compiled store keeps version 39, so a newer component store still
replaces it; the blocklist is merged into every CRLSet and holds whichever store is active.

